--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.mem.class]/1, [class.nest]/3: a member class of a class template
may be defined outside the class template by a qualified name, here from
outside its namespace (`template <class C> struct ns::S<C>::N { ... };').
The front end grafts an out-of-class member class definition into the class
template only for the form `S<C>::N' (cpp_typecheck_template.cpp, "single-
level qualification only"); the namespace-qualified form is ignored, S<char>::N
stays incomplete and f's body is left without N.  Defining it inside the
namespace works (cpp_member_class_defined_after_instantiation/
test_namespace.desc).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
